    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14733" root="رتم" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرُّ تُرْتُمٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُرْتَمٌ</span> <i>Continual,</i> or <i>constant, evil:</i>
(K, TA:) the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">م</span> is a substitute for the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ب</span> of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُرْتَُب</span>; and the former <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span> is augmentative, because
there is no word like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُعْفَرٌ</span> consisting of radical
letters. (TA.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَاتِمًا</span>, above.]

